## General layout for Euler-Lagrange with Lagrange multipliers
> Adapted from  
section 7.5  
Stephen T. Thornton and Jerry B. Marion. Classical Dynamics of Particles and Systems. Fifth. Thomson Brooks/Cole, 2004.

In general, the Euler-Lagrange equation with multipliers is written as

$$
\boxed{
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d} t} \frac{\partial}{\partial \dot{q_i}} \mathcal{L} 
- \frac{\partial}{\partial q_i} \mathcal{L} 
= \sum_k \lambda_k(t) \frac{\partial}{\partial q_i} f_k
}
\quad
\left\{
  \begin{array}{l}
  i= 1,2,\dots,n \quad \text{generalized coordinates} \\
  k= 1,2,\dots,p \quad \text{constraints}
  \end{array}
\right.
$$
where
$$
\sum_K F^\text{constraint}_{k}
=
\sum_k \lambda_k(t) \frac{\partial}{\partial q_i} f_k
,
$$
is the sum of all generalized forces needed to guarantee the $f_k$ constraints.

